Chapter 3

AWR‑Mars: Autonomous Walking Industrial Rover

3.1 System Architecture

The AWR‑Mars (Autonomous Walking Rover – Industrial) is a heavy‑lift quadrupedal platform that serves as the primary manufacturing agent in the MSAT triad. Its core mission is the production of capital goods—structural steel, tool heads, machine components, and ultimately, additional rover chassis—from raw Martian materials. The platform must simultaneously meet three demanding requirements:

1. Industrial payload: manipulate tool heads of up to 120 kg with sub‑millimetre positioning accuracy.
2. Locomotion: traverse unprepared regolith with slopes up to 25° while carrying a 400 kg payload.
3. Manufacturing: host a mobile foundry capable of producing 100 kg of steel per sol.

