Integration into AIADN. The terrain classifier runs on each rover's dedicated vision processor at 10 Hz. Classification outputs feed into a 3D occupancy grid maintained by the AIADN Layer 1 mesh. The global path planner (modified A*) computes energy-optimal routes that avoid hazardous terrain while respecting the 5 m minimum separation between rovers. Local obstacle avoidance runs at 100 Hz using a model-predictive contouring control formulation.

6.8 Communication Architecture and Delay-Tolerant Networking

